    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0358" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg348"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Secretary to the Admiralty to Mr. Hammond.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiralty,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 26, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am commanded by my lords commissioners of
                    the admiralty to send you herewith, for the information of Earl Russell, a copy
                    of a letter from Rear-Admiral Sir Baldwin Walker, dated the 19th August, with
                    copies of its enclosures, relative to the proceedings of vessels-of-war of the
                    so-styled Confederate States of North America at the Cape of Good Hope.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. G ROMAINE</signed></closer>














